course: dictionary
lesson: 13385
title: Comparing with -er words
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Healthier is the comparing form of healthy. We use it when we put two things side by side and say which one is better for your health. «Water is healthier than fizzy drinks.» Healthy means good for your body, so healthier means more healthy: it is the better choice of the two.
explain: Look for the word «than» after it. «Fruit is a healthier snack than sweets» compares fruit with sweets, and the sentence tells you which one wins. When you see -er on the end of a describing word, ask yourself: is this comparing two things?
explain: Healthier can also come before a noun, as in «a healthier option» or «a healthier lifestyle». No second thing is named there, but the idea of comparing is still there: it is better than the usual choice.
fact: Healthy is the base word; healthier is the comparing form for two things; healthiest is the top form for three or more.
fact: Healthier means more healthy, so it usually compares two things, often with «than».
fact: Words ending in -y change the y to i before -er: happy, happier; healthy, healthier.
fact: «Healthier choice» means the better choice for your body.
fact: Healthier does not mean perfectly healthy; it only means better for you than the other thing.
exercise: «Water is healthier than fizzy drinks.» What does healthier mean here? | Bigger in size | Sweeter and more fun | *Better for your health | Colder and wetter
exercise: «Walking is ___ than sitting all day.» Choose the right word to fill the gap. | *healthier | healthy | healthiest | health
exercise: Which sentence uses healthier correctly? | *Apples are healthier than crisps. | Apples are more healthier than crisps. | Apples are healthy than crisps. | Apples are healthiest than crisps.
test: Which word means more healthy? | *healthier | health | unhealthy | healthy
test: Which word best finishes this sentence: «Swimming is ___ than watching TV.» | *healthier | healthiest | heavier | healthy
exam: Which phrase means the better choice for your body? | *a healthier choice | a health choice | a healthy choicer | a more healthier choice
